native (post-norm ON) curve at every theta -- more sensitive to rotation once the real
mechanism is removed -- and shifts toward the Qwen/Llama native curves specifically, not
just away from Gemma's own native curve in some arbitrary direction. If the BYPASSED curve
barely moves, post-norm alone doesn't explain Gemma's invariance and Real Check #2 below
(the dilution ratio, independent of any specific normalization submodule) is doing more of
the explanatory work.

