downward-sloping ratio-vs-cos.sim curve (higher relative branch magnitude -> more
disruption), even though each model reaches different (ratio, theta) pairs -- that would
be evidence the relationship is a property of the dilution ratio itself, not of any one
architecture. If instead the three models trace clearly SEPARATE curves at the SAME ratio
value, dilution alone doesn't explain the cross-model gap, and something architecture-
specific (e.g. Gemma's post-norm, tested causally in Real Check #1 above) is doing
additional explanatory work beyond what the ratio alone captures.

