orbit-like near-returns), the CKA-vs-theta curve at the rotated layer, or immediately
downstream, should also be non-monotonic, roughly tracking the accuracy dip/recovery.
If CKA instead degrades monotonically while accuracy does not, the recovery is happening
in how the (still-corrupted) representation is READ OUT, not in the representation itself.

